Anatomy of a Jig (Four Parts, One Tool)
​DEF NAME  
​Concept: The jig's part number, stamped on the side. Chosen so a stranger knows what it does.  
​PARAMETERS  
​Concept: The clamps. Whatever you fit in becomes the workpiece for this run — and only this run.  
​BODY  
​Concept: The operations, indented under the def line. Written once, however many times it runs.  
​RETURN  
​Concept: The finished part handed back to the bench. Without it, the jig keeps its work to itself.  
​Code Implementation & Function Invocationdef inspect(dia, lower=24.95, upper=25.05):  # defaults = standard setting
    if dia > upper:
        return "REWORK"
    elif dia < lower:
        return "SCRAP"
    return "ACCEPT"

inspect(25.02)                   # "ACCEPT" - standard tolerance
inspect(25.02, 25.00, 25.04)    # "REWORK" - tighter job, positional
inspect(25.02, upper=25.01)     # "REWORK" - keyword: change ONE setting
